# Marketing surface — Cloudflare Pages routing parity (DEPLOY.md §3, vercel.json).
#
# Cloudflare evaluates these top-to-bottom, first match wins. Existing static
# assets (hashed /assets/*, index.html, fonts) are served as files BEFORE the
# 200 SPA rewrite, so the catch-all only handles client-side routes. Keep the
# SPA fallback LAST.
#
# Copied into dist/ at deploy time by marketing-cloudflare.yml (not in public/).

# Privilege boundary — /console is a SEPARATE, privileged origin. Hard 308 so a
# deep marketing link to the console lands on console.acgs.ai, never a
# marketing-side render. Marketing.tsx's "Open the console" CTA points at the
# absolute console URL in production; this is defense-in-depth (DEPLOY.md §3).
/console        https://console.acgs.ai/console          308
/console/*      https://console.acgs.ai/console/:splat    308

# Internal docs must 404, never fall through to the SPA shell. The marketing
# build already strips these (vite removeInternalDocs); this matches vercel.json's
# explicit 404 posture as defense-in-depth.
/AGENTS.md      /404.html   404
/CLAUDE.md      /404.html   404
/DESIGN.md      /404.html   404
/DEPLOY.md      /404.html   404

# SPA client-side routing fallback — MUST stay last.
/*              /index.html  200
